Third-party notices for Hoverdock
=================================

LibreHardwareMonitor (Intel / AMD CPU package temperature algorithm)
--------------------------------------------------------------
Portions of the native CPU package-temperature path in src/SystemTemps.cpp
follow LibreHardwareMonitor's IntelCpu (IA32_TEMPERATURE_TARGET,
IA32_PACKAGE_THERM_STATUS, TjMax - digital readout) and Amd17Cpu (SMN
THM_TCON_CUR_TMP / Tctl/Tdie decode, including early-Zen Tctl offsets).

  https://github.com/LibreHardwareMonitor/LibreHardwareMonitor
  License: Mozilla Public License 2.0 / Apache License 2.0

PawnIO IntelMSR + AMDFamily17 modules (third_party/pawnio/)
----------------------------------------------------------
Signed PawnIO AMX blobs used to read whitelisted Intel MSRs and AMD Zen
SMN registers via the PawnIO kernel driver (\\?\GLOBALROOT\Device\PawnIO).
Redistributed from LibreHardwareMonitorLib resources / namazso
PawnIO.Modules releases (AMDFamily17.bin from release 0.2.11).

  https://github.com/namazso/PawnIO.Modules
  https://pawnio.eu/
  License: GNU LGPL 2.1 (see third_party/pawnio/COPYING)

The PawnIO driver itself is a separate system install (not bundled with
Hoverdock). Opening the device typically requires an elevated process on
Windows; Hoverdock uses a one-time elevated scheduled task that runs
Dock.exe --cpu-sensor (same binary, no .NET helper).

AMD Display Library (ADL) — runtime only
----------------------------------------
AMD GPU temperature and board/ASIC watts are read by dynamically loading
atiadlxx.dll from the AMD graphics driver (ADL2_Main_Control_Create,
ADL2_New_QueryPMLogData_Get, Overdrive5/6 fallbacks). The ADL SDK headers /
library are not redistributed; only documented public exports are used at
runtime when an AMD GPU driver is installed.

  https://gpuopen.com/adl/
